/* The location purpose string iOS shows when Doorprints first asks for location (CMP-8b; Hunt mode since S4b-BL-69):
   placing a saved house, planning visits from here and, with Hunt mode on, the alert when you pass a saved house, in
   the words of the app's own strings (android/ui composeResources: house_use_location, ai_plan_location_off,
   map_hunt_notify_rationale). Keep Info.plist's English value the same. */
"NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription" = "Doorprints uses your location to place the houses you save, to plan visits from where you are and, while Hunt mode is on, to tell you when you pass a house you have saved.";

/* Shown when Doorprints first reaches a server on the local network (a LAN IP address or a .local name, CMP-8b).
   Keep Info.plist's English value the same. */
"NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription" = "Doorprints connects to your own Doorprints server when it is on your local network.";
"NSFaceIDUsageDescription" = "Doorprints uses Face ID to unlock the app when the app lock is on.";

/* The "Always" purpose string (S4b-BL-96, the area wake-up), shown when Wake me in my hunting areas asks for location
   all the time; the when-in-use uses first, in the same words, then the wake-up (area_wakeup_why, area_wakeup_what_ios).
   Keep Info.plist's English value the same. */
"NSLocationAlwaysAndWhenInUseUsageDescription" = "Doorprints uses your location to place the houses you save, to plan visits from where you are and, while Hunt mode is on, to tell you when you pass a house you have saved. With Wake me in my hunting areas on, iOS also tells Doorprints when you arrive in one of your areas, so it can offer Hunt mode. Doorprints keeps no location history.";

/* S4b-BL-81: the name of the backup document type (Info.plist CFBundleDocumentTypes). */
"Doorprints backup" = "Doorprints backup";
